plex connections (cognitive competence).\n- Weaknesses: unfriendly (crew cooperation, communication), eats unhealthily (maybe health, reliability), sometimes not good at taking criticism (cooperation), can be unorganized (reliability), regarded as a show-off (communication), not open to new ideas (adaptability), maybe not open to feedback.\n\nOverall: strong technical and leadership, but significant cooperation and reliability concerns.\n\nCandidate B:\n- Strengths: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), good technical competence.\n- Weaknesses: regarded as pretentious (communication), sometimes adopts wrong tone (communication), can be grumpy (communication), can be uncooperative (crew cooperation), makes nasty remarks (communication), relatively weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy).\n\nOverall: strong reliability and stress, but communication and cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate C:\n- Strengths: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation, responsibility), excellent attention skills (attention), 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (cooperation), keeps calm in crisis (stress), understands complicated technology (technical), excellent attention skills (already), puts concern for others (responsibility).\n- Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (cooperation), not very willing to further his education (adaptability), maybe egocentric conflicts with positive atmosphere? But we have positive crew atmosphere.\n\nOverall: strong reliability, decision, stress, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric.\n\nCandidate D:\n- Strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), takes responsibility seriously, problem solving, concentration.\n- Weaknesses: considered moody (cooperation), regarded as a loner (cooperation), regarded as arrogant (communication), relatively weak leadership skills (crew cooperation), hot temper (communication), know-it-all (communication), moody.\n\nOverall: strong technical and responsibility, but cooperation and communication issues.\n\nNow we need to decide which candidate best fits overall. The panel must consider all criteria, not overvalue one strength.\n\nCandidate C seems to have many strengths across reliability, decision, stress, crew atmosphere, attention, technical, and responsibility (concern for others). The main weaknesses are communication difficulty and egocentric, but also positive crew atmosphere suggests he can work well with crew despite egocentric? The egocentric may conflict with crew cooperation, but the positive atmosphere may mitigate. Also not willing to further education may affect adaptability, but maybe less critical.\n\nCandidate B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues (pretentious, wrong tone, nasty remarks) and weak memory for numbers (attention). That could be serious for safety.\n\nCandidate D has strong technical and responsibility, but many cooperation and communication issues (moody, loner, arrogant, hot temper). Likely less suitable.\n\nCandidate A has strong technical and leadership, but unfriendly, unorganized, not open to new ideas, etc.\n\nThus Candidate C appears strongest overall, with reliability, decision quality, stress, crew atmosphere, attention, technical competence. The communication difficulty is a concern but may be trainable. Egocentric may be mitigated by his concern for others and positive atmosphere.\n\nThus as Sofia, I might shift my recommendation to Candidate C, aligning with Agent 1's recommendation, and argue that the reliability fact (100% reliable) is decisive, and that B's communication issues are more severe (nasty remarks) than C's difficulty communicating ideas.\n\nAlternatively, I could stay with B, but I think the panel should converge on C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 3 originally recommended B, Agent 1 recommended C, Agent 2 defended B. Now I need to respond, perhaps agreeing with Agent 1 and challenging Agent 2's claim that B's reliability outweighs C's. I can point out that we have explicit reliability for C (100% reliable) and also positive crew atmosphere, while B's communication issues are more severe (nasty remarks, pretentious). Also B's weak memory for numbers is a safety risk.\n\nThus I will change my vote to Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: concise, referencing prior points, citing facts: C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, excellent attention, puts concern for others. B's nasty remarks, weak memory for numbers, pretentious, wrong tone. Conclude C is best.\n\nMetadata: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
